==English==

===Etymology===
{{prefix|in|numerable|lang=en}}; from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|innumérable}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|innumerabilis}}, from {{prefix|in|numerabilis|lang=la|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-innumerable.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɪn.nuːmɜːɹ.æbəl/|lang=en}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɪˈnjuːməɹ.əbəl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Not capable of being [[counted]], [[enumerated]], or [[numbered]], hence, indefinitely numerous; of great number.
#: {{ux|en|The casualties of the Second World War were so great that they are '''innumerable'''.}}
#* {{w|Mark Twain}}, ''A Connecticut Yankee in King Arthur's Court''
#*: Soon we could see the '''innumerable''' banners fluttering, and then the sun struck the sea of armor and set it all aflash.

